00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:29.512
<v NARRATOR>Bramble met Boom on a blustery evening, and he heard him before he saw him. A creature was telling a story across the circle, and every single word came out at exactly the same loudness.

4
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:47.483
<v NARRATOR>"And the giant stomped and the bridge shook and everyone ran and it was very exciting." Said all on one flat level, it just washed over the listeners like rain on a roof. The big giant landed like a small mouse.

5
00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:53.294
<v BOOM>All one size. A story can't be all one size.

6
00:00:53.294 --> 00:00:57.705
<v NARRATOR>Bramble hopped over. "What do you mean, one size?"

7
00:00:57.705 --> 00:01:07.716
<v BOOM>Watch — or, listen. Once... there was a sound in the dark that nobody could explain.

8
00:01:07.716 --> 00:01:18.087
<v NARRATOR>He breathed it so softly that Bramble had to lean right in to catch it. The whisper had reeled him in like a fish on a line.

9
00:01:18.087 --> 00:01:28.058
<v BOOM>And it was the SEA, my friends — the whole wide SEA, come all the way up the valley to say hello!

10
00:01:28.058 --> 00:01:33.789
<v NARRATOR>Bramble jumped. The loud part had surprised him, in the best way.

11
00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:44.520
<v BOOM>My name is Boom. Soft pulls them close. Loud wakes them up. You point at the important parts with your volume.

12
00:01:44.520 --> 00:02:02.051
<v BRAMBLE>I run a listening-circle, and the kids tell their tales all one flat size — every word the same. Their giants are tiny and their whispers are gone. Would you teach them to change their size?

13
00:02:02.051 --> 00:02:19.782
<v BOOM>Gladly. But here's the secret they miss: the loud part only works because of all the soft parts around it. One big BOOM after a long quiet stretch lands like thunder. A story that shouts the whole time is just noise.

14
00:02:19.782 --> 00:02:27.233
<v NARRATOR>Bramble felt it was true — the whisper and the boom were partners, not rivals.

15
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:37.204
<v BOOM>So don't be loud. Be loud on purpose, in one place, and let the quiet make it matter. That's how you point.

16
00:02:37.204 --> 00:02:51.895
<v NARRATOR>And around the fire that night, the tellers found their sizes — a whisper to pull close, a boom to wake them up — and their giants, at last, grew tall.

